            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> That's fair. Perhaps a `flushleft` field in the `setup` argument table that takes a _user-supplied_ array of filetypes? E.g.,\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> require('mini.comment').setup{\r\n>   flushleft = { 'asciidoc' }\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nA step up, but still not the way I would like it to be supported.\r\n\r\nI am right now toying with the idea of allowing buffer-local variable with *Lua pattern* defining comment. This should allow more flexibility with a relatively small code overhead. Not sure yet that it will be implemented, though.",
